## Open questions for THIS table (ranked)
- **Q1 (the one that matters): the w→0 limit of the hybrid architecture.** R ~ 40/w² and k grow polynomially;
  the cut grows e^{c/w} but only as bulk. What does the w→0 limit of the hybrid chain LOOK like as a single
  statement? Is there a formulation where the polynomial-structure part converges to a closed object
  (an operator inequality, a density statement) while the bulk is absorbed — i.e., can "R≈40/w² resonant
  terms + directional bound" be written as ONE w-uniform inequality? What fails if RH is false? (Gate:
  state it or it dies.)
- **Q2: why 40/w² — derive the quadratic.** R·w² ≈ 40 on [14,44]. Candidate reading: R ~ (envelope width in
  u = 2/w) × (slots per unit u = 1/Bragg spacing s/2π) × band factor? Predicts the constant's band/T
  dependence — testable immediately. A DERIVED count law would be the first a-priori piece of the
  structure side.
- **Q3: the collective object's true nature.** The tail behaves as one smooth PNT object with tiny
  fluctuation (measured). Is B_collective = arch − T_smooth (density-minus-density) a NAMED object in the
  Gabor/de Branges/Toeplitz world? The §335 fluctuation identity says arch-density − primes = zeros-density;
  the collective chain is that identity USED as a certificate. Does the frame-theory literature (BGL,
  Seip) have a w-uniform version of exactly this comparison?
- **Q4: the s↔γ calibration + involution.** Measured law log n* ≈ 2π/s. Calibrate s (probe spacing) to γ
  (band height) at criticality: is the major-arc set closed under n ↔ γ/2πn? Either branch banked as a gain
  (closed → pairing halves the check; open → sieve absorbs). Dirac's retraction stands until this lands.
- **Q5 (guard, run early): conservativity of the hybrid statement.** "The hybrid chain certifies to the rank
  limit for all (w, band)" — as w→0 this must become RH-equivalent (test class completes). WHERE does the
  statement stop being provable-per-config and start being the wall? Name the exact quantifier switch. If
  the answer is "the R~40/w² structure is per-config but its w-uniformity is conservative-equivalent to
  RH," say so plainly and aim Q1 accordingly.

